# GMEOW native vs ELK/HermiT DL/EL crosscheck ledger.
# Built from the native EL/DL reasoning lane ONLY (Java/Docker-free). The
# oracle comparison runs in the classic-cross-check lane; DlGap rows are
# native coverage defects and the committed bundle must keep gapCount at 0.
# DO NOT EDIT.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .

# --- ledger header (native coverage; #697 gap-zero) ---
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/dl-el-crosscheck> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/CrosscheckLedger> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/consistent> true ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/oracleCrosscheck> "classic-cross-check confirms the native result; DlGap is a failure"@en .

# --- native-only subsumption entailments ---
